an determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $x=uv$ and $y=\\frac{v}{u}.$ \n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =v & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =u \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =-\\frac{v}{{u}^{2}} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =\\frac{1}{u}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}v & u \\\\ -\\frac{v}{{u}^{2}}\\, & \\frac{1}{u}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =v\\cdot \\frac{1}{u}\\text{ }-u\\cdot (-\\frac{v}{{u}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2v}{u}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, when $[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],$ the value of our Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n{\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(-2,3)}=\\frac{2(3)}{-2}=-3.\n$$" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321388 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321389 13194139534943 true] [17592186321388 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321390 13194139534943 true] [17592186321388 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321391 13194139534943 true] [17592186321388 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321392 13194139534943 true] [17592186321388 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321393 13194139534943 true] [17592186321388 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534943 true] [17592186321388 1041 "selection" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321388 1104 #edb/ref 17592186321393 13194139534943 true] [17592186321388 1110 #uuid "fdd4d8e8-ebdd-5a44-b693-2dc6b1d9eca2" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321389 1034 "3" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321389 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534943 true] [17592186321389 1111 #uuid "4b2d0948-335e-5a83-935d-32686d857beb" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321390 1034 "2" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321390 110