\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321430 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321431 13194139534943 true] [17592186321430 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321432 13194139534943 true] [17592186321430 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321433 13194139534943 true] [17592186321430 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321434 13194139534943 true] [17592186321430 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321435 13194139534943 true] [17592186321430 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534943 true] [17592186321430 1041 "selection" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321430 1104 #edb/ref 17592186321434 13194139534943 true] [17592186321430 1110 #uuid "65f2f7c7-8a7d-52df-9828-dafeed9e1231" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321431 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\delta A" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321431 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534943 true] [17592186321431 1111 #uuid "f51e42d0-86fc-55a9-a8d9-ed171e4f1106" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321432 1034 "3\\,\\delta A" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321432 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534943 true] [17592186321432 1111 #uuid "b8a816e2-c515-596e-8328-fe3491451466" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321433 1034 "4\\,\\delta A" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321433 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534943 true] [17592186321433 1111 #uuid "d8f626c7-2bf0-5ecc-93cb-3fd24b7dd656" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321434 1034 "2\\,\\delta A" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321434 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534943 true] [17592186321434 1111 #uuid "ecfb9684-e70c-53ca-87d1-ce22a81bb026" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321435 1034 "\\delta A" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321435 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534943 true] [17592186321435 1111 #uuid "c9e0e9b2-1ba5-501d-a03d-a02b6abd70ed" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321436 1017 #edb/ref 17592186321437 13194139534943 true] [17592186321436 1089 "q-161837" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321436 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534943 true] [17592186321436 1100 "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3}+v \\\\ uv\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-reversing?" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321436 1113 #uuid "c2f0da55-1926-59a4-96c8-e68855af7a42" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321436 1145 "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing at the points where the Jacobian determinant is negative:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}<0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3}+v \\\\ uv\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2} & 1 \\\\ v & u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & ={u}^{2}\\cdot u-v\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={u}^{3}-v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{3}-v & <0 \\\\ v & >{u}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv={u}^{3}\n$$\n\ndefines a cubic function, and the coordinates of, say, $(-1,1)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing must be the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043620/assets/cb5b22ff46569b231d122c2ed11bd412907f36271a033d86769435adf9fe48c7.png)" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321437 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321438 13194139534943 true] [17592186321437 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321439 13194139534943 true] [17592186321437 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321440 13194139534943 true] [17592186321437 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321441 13194139534943 true] [17592186321437 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321442 13194139534943 true] [17592186321437 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534943 true] [17592186321437 1041 "selection" 13194139534943 