943 true] [17592186321478 1100 "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(2,4)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{u}^{2}}{v} \\\\ uv\\end{aligned}]?\n$$" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321478 1113 #uuid "8da66ba0-baf0-55db-8a40-0cff8a5bd366" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321478 1145 "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot {{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{⏟}}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2u}{v} & -\\frac{{u}^{2}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\ v & u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{2u}{v}\\cdot u-v\\cdot (-\\frac{{u}^{2}}{{v}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2{u}^{2}}{v}+\\frac{{u}^{2}}{v} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{u}^{2}}{v} \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(2,4)} & =(\\frac{3{u}^{2}}{v})\\,{|}_{u=2\\,v=4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(2)^{2}}{4} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|3|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =3\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321479 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321480 13194139534943 true] [17592186321479 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321481 13194139534943 true] [17592186321479 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321482 13194139534943 true] [17592186321479 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321483 13194139534943 true] [17592186321479 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321484 13194139534943 true] [17592186321479 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534943 true] [17592186