 true] [17592186321485 1145 "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot {{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{⏟}}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{v}}{2\\sqrt{u}} & \\frac{\\sqrt{u}}{2\\sqrt{v}} \\\\ {v}^{2} & 2uv\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{v}}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot 2uv-{v}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{u}}{2\\sqrt{v}} \\\\  & =v\\sqrt{uv}-\\frac{1}{2}v\\sqrt{uv} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}v\\sqrt{uv} \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(1,4)} & ={(\\frac{1}{2}v\\sqrt{uv})\\,|}_{u=1\\,v=4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4)\\sqrt{(1)(4)} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|4|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =4\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321486 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321487 13194139534943 true] [17592186321486 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321488 13194139534943 true] [17592186321486 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321489 13194139534943 true] [17592186321486 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321490 13194139534943 true] [17592186321486 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321491 13194139534943 true] [17592186321486 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534943 true] [17592186321486 1041 "selection" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321486 1104 #edb/ref 17592186321490 13194139534943 true] [17592186321486 1110 #uuid "d4a27b2d-ad2d-51d5-8728-36f4074f18dc" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321487 1034 "12\\,\\delta A" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321487 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534943 true] [17592186321487 1111 #uuid "d1b8aca2-a24d-5291-9ff4-ef0374976569" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321488 1034 "8\\,\\delta A" 13194139534943 true] [17592186321488 1103 #edb/ref 1759218604